#@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
#@type = "zendesk.frontend"

Feature: Zendesk Large File Attachment As Partner
	Testing the large file uploader as partner in Zendesk.

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Lfapar - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I teardown tickets requested by the users with the following email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| lfa.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	| lfa.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Lfapar - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Lfazen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| LFAPARLFAPAR |
	| LFAZENLFAZEN |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| LFAPARLFAPAR |
	| LFAZENLFAZEN |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| lfa.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	| lfa.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| lfa.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	| lfa.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| lfa.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	| lfa.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| lfa.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	| lfa.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| New Subscription(s) for Lfapar - ${staticProjectName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Lfazen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| lfa.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	| lfa.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Lfapar - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Lfazen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: Upload large file
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	Users should be able to upload large attachments to a ticket using the large file uploader as a partner

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I get all test passwords and admin emails
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | lfa.partner1                      |
	| Email Address | lfa.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| First Name    | LFA                               |
	| Last Name     | Partner1                          |
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | lfa.partner2                      |
	| Email Address | lfa.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| First Name    | LFA                               |
	| Last Name     | Partner2                          |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Name   | Lfapar - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Code   | LFAPARLFAPAR                  | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Lfapar - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Service Partnership" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Partner"
	And I assign the contact with the email address "lfa.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" on the account "Lfapar - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Partner Member |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "lfa.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" on the account "Lfapar - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Partner Manager |
	And I create an assigned team nested field for a team with the name "Lfapar - ${staticProjectName}" assigned to the account "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | lfa.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | LFA                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Assigned Team Nested Field | ${staticAssignedTeamNestedField} | |
	| Code                       | LFAZENLFAZEN                     | |
	| Data Region                | United States                    | |
	| Language                   | English                          | |
	| Name                       | Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}    | |
	| Region                     | United States                    | |
	| Status                     | Active                           | |
	| Tier                       | T1                               | |
	And I assign the team with the name "Lfapar - ${staticProjectName}" on the account "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Partner |
	And I assign the team with the name "Lfapar - ${staticProjectName}" on the account "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| First Line Support |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Requester |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Portal Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 6 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Gold Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Partner"
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the support organization with the code "LFAZENLFAZEN" should be part of the support site
	And the organization "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the support user with the email address "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "lfa.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "lfa.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the user with the email address "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "lfa.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "lfa.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	When I update the support password for user with the email address "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "lfa.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "lfa.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I update the user with the email address "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to use the password "zendeskqauser"
	And I update the user with the email address "lfa.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" to use the password "zendeskqauser"
	And I update the user with the email address "lfa.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" to use the password "zendeskqauser"
	And I log into zendesk as "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I create a request with the following values
	| Product       | Liferay Portal                          | 6.2                                   |
	| Component     | Activation Key & Project Administration |                                       |
	| System Status | Production                              | Functioning with limited capabilities |
	| Subject       | Request Subject                         |                                       |
	| Description   | Request Description                     |                                       |
	| Attachments   | Document_1.txt                          |                                       |
	Then I should be able to view a request with the following details
	| Subject       | Request Subject                                    |
	| Status        | OPEN                                               |
	| Requester     | LFA Customer1                                      |
	| Priority      | Normal                                             |
	| Product       | Liferay Portal > 6.2                               |
	| Sub-Status    | —                                                  |
	| Component     | Activation Key & Project Administration            |
	| System Status | Production > Functioning with limited capabilities |
	| Attachments   | Document_1.txt                                     |
	And I should be able to view a request comment containing the text "Request Description" with the following details
	| Author      | LFA Customer1       |
	| Comment     | Request Description |
	| Attachments | Document_1.txt      |
	When I log out and log into the support homepage as "lfa.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I log into zendesk as "lfa.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I go to the request with the ID "${staticRequestId}"
	And I accept all cookies
	And I upload a file using the large file uploader with the following parameters
	| Attachment       | Document_2.txt      |
	| Comment          | Large File Comment1 |
	| Data Region      | United States       |
	| No Personal Data | false               |
	Then I should be able to view a large file comment containing the text "Large File Comment1" with the following details
	| Author      | LFA Partner1 [P]    |
	| Comment     | Large File Comment1 |
	| Attachment  | Document_2.txt      |
	When I log out and log into the support homepage as "lfa.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I log into zendesk as "lfa.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I go to the request with the ID "${staticRequestId}"
	And I accept all cookies
	And I upload a file using the large file uploader with the following parameters
	| Attachment       | Document_3.txt      |
	| Comment          | Large File Comment2 |
	| Data Region      | United States       |
	| No Personal Data | false               |
	Then I should be able to view a large file comment containing the text "Large File Comment2" with the following details
	| Author      | LFA Partner2 [P]    |
	| Comment     | Large File Comment2 |
	| Attachment  | Document_3.txt      |
	And I should be able to view a large file comment containing the text "Large File Comment1" with the following details
	| Author      | LFA Partner1 [P]    |
	| Comment     | Large File Comment1 |
	| Attachment  | Document_2.txt      |
	When I go to the Project Details page
	And I go to the project with the name "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the Attachments tab
	Then the attachment with the keyword "Document_3.txt" should be visible with the following values
	| Ticket                         | ${staticRequestId} |
	| File Name                      | Document_3.txt     |
	| File Name Link                 | false              |
	| File Size                      | 1KB                |
	| Attached                       | LFA Partner2       |
	| Does Not Contain Personal Data | false              |
	And the attachment with the keyword "Document_3.txt" should have the actions link visible
	Then the attachment with the keyword "Document_2.txt" should be visible with the following values
	| Ticket                         | ${staticRequestId} |
	| File Name                      | Document_2.txt     |
	| File Name Link                 | false              |
	| File Size                      | 1KB                |
	| Attached                       | LFA Partner1       |
	| Does Not Contain Personal Data | false              |
	And the attachment with the keyword "Document_2.txt" should not have the actions or delete link visible
	When I log out and log into the support homepage as "lfa.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	And I go to the project with the name "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the Attachments tab
	Then the attachment with the keyword "Document_3.txt" should be visible with the following values
	| Ticket                         | ${staticRequestId} |
	| File Name                      | Document_3.txt     |
	| File Name Link                 | false              |
	| File Size                      | 1KB                |
	| Attached                       | LFA Partner2       |
	| Does Not Contain Personal Data | false              |
	And the attachment with the keyword "Document_3.txt" should not have the actions or delete link visible
	Then the attachment with the keyword "Document_2.txt" should be visible with the following values
	| Ticket                         | ${staticRequestId} |
	| File Name                      | Document_2.txt     |
	| File Name Link                 | false              |
	| File Size                      | 1KB                |
	| Attached                       | LFA Partner1       |
	| Does Not Contain Personal Data | false              |
	And the attachment with the keyword "Document_2.txt" should have the actions link visible